    test(match): the constants live in the baseline, so read them there
    
    Three assertions still read the compact hot frame after the previous commit:
      * pool: drawnDisabledBonds / bannedChess -> read the baseline the seat was sent;
      * realtime: the throttle cadence is asserted over the hot frames only (the baseline is one
        extra frame per join/resync and is not throttled), while the phase set still counts every
        frame - a short presentation phase can arrive in a baseline alone;
      * connection: already updated in the previous commit.

